662	    beats
663	      ? `   - Return EXACTLY ${beats.length} scenes matching the beats above, in order. Scene N visualizes ONLY what beat N says — read its words and illustrate them literally.`
664	      : `   - A watchable reel holds each idea ~3.5 to 4.5 seconds so viewers can process it. Cut this script into approximately ${targetSceneCount} visual shots (between ${Math.max(4, targetSceneCount - 2)} and ${targetSceneCount + 2} scenes).`,
665	    '   - Every scene holds 4-14 spoken words. NEVER group 15+ words into one slow scene; NEVER emit 1-2 word flash scenes.',
666	    '2. VISUAL DIVERSITY (ANTI-REPETITION — STRICTLY ENFORCED):',
667	    '   - NEVER use the same visual twice in a row. Rotate across at least 4 different visuals per reel.',
668	    '   - Match the visual to THIS topic (not to tech by default):',
669	    '     - kinetic_typography: 2-5 word hook slammed huge (opening + punchlines).',
670	    '     - bento_grid / stat_spotlight: stats, numbers, facts, impacts.',
671	    '     - comparison_matrix / split_screen: before-vs-after, myth-vs-fact, option A vs B.',
672	    '     - timeline_path: sequences, journeys, steps, evolution.',
673	    '     - quote_card: memorable one-liner or verdict.',
674	    '     - dialogue_cards / sticker_collage: reactions, voices, comedy beats.',
675	    '     - neural_flow / radial_gauge / architecture_stack / terminal_stream: ONLY for genuinely technical topics with real data payloads.',
676	    '     - cinematic_* / landscape_canvas: ONLY when a photo is supplied for this scene.',
677	    '   - Copy the topic vocabulary into visualData (elements/bars/nodes/metric). NEVER write AGI/AI-brain placeholder copy for non-tech topics.',
678	    beats
679	      ? '3. VOICE SYNC (ALREADY SOLVED — DO NOT TOUCH):'
680	      : '3. VOICE SYNC (SERVER-ENFORCED, YOU PROVIDE HINTS):',
681	    beats
682	      ? '   - "narrationBeat" MUST be the beat text copied word-for-word. The timestamps already sync audio, mouth, and cuts.'
683	      : '   - For EVERY scene, provide "narrationBeat": roughly which consecutive words are spoken during that cut (4-14 words).',
684	    beats
685	      ? '   - NEVER invent words outside the beats. If a beat is a personal line ("my sister"), use kinetic_typography, quote_card, or dialogue_cards — never a data chart.'
686	      : '   - The server re-partitions beats onto the script EXACTLY, so keep beats in script order and proportional — do not invent words outside the script.',
687	    '4. TEXT DISCIPLINE (OVERFLOW KILLS READABILITY):',
688	    '   - kicker: 1-3 words. headline: 2-8 words, a LABEL — never the full spoken sentence.',
689	    '   - body: 1 short sentence (<=28 words) supporting the visual.',
690	    '   - NEVER set headline identical to narrationBeat (no double text on screen).',
691	    '5. RICH MOTION GRAPHICS DATA (EVERY DATA VISUAL MUST EAT REAL WORDS):',
692	    '   - For EVERY bento_grid / stat_spotlight / comparison_matrix / split_screen / radial_gauge / timeline_path / architecture_stack / neural_flow scene, visualData MUST be copied from that scene\'s beat words: numbers ("9 hours", "90%"), named effects ("shrinking attention", "spiking anxiety"), steps in order.',
